   "title": "N. Korea slams multination statement backing anti-Pyongyang sanctions as 'strategic failure'",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/foreignaffairs/northkorea/20261031/n-korea-slams-multination-statement-backing-anti-pyongyang-sanctions-as-strategic-failure",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:42:04 GMT",
   "_dt": 1793414524.0,
   "ageDays": 0.02,
   "summary": "A spokesperson from the North's foreign ministry issued the criticism in a statement, after 11 countries and the European Union (EU) released the joint statement earlier this week reaffirming their commitment to monitoring the North's activities in violation of U.N. Security Council (UNSC) sanctions resolutions.",
   "summary_zh": "北方外交部发言人在一份声明中提出批评。此前，11个国家和欧洲联盟（EU）于本周早些时候发表联合声明，再次承诺监督北方违反联合国安全理事会（UNSC）制裁决议的活动。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "A spokesperson from the North's foreign ministry issued the criticism in a statement, after 11 countries and the European Union (EU) released the joint statement earlier this week reaffirming their commitment to monitoring the North's activities in violation of U.N. Security Council (UNSC) sanctions resolutions. The joint statement also highlighted the findings of the Multilateral Sanctions Monitoring Team (MSMT) on the North's illicit activities and welcomed fresh independent sanctions imposed by the U.S., Australia and the EU over the North's cyberactivities and dispatch of its workers overseas to finance its nuclear weapons and missile programs. \"This is another case that reminds us that the hostile forces' bad habit of denying the constitutional status of our state,\" the spokesperson said in the statement carried by the North's Korean Central News Agency. \"The isolated are not us but the U.S. and the Western camp which have lost judgment and courage to admit their strategic failure despite the lack of their means and ability to prove the effectiveness of their sanctions,\" the official said. The official went on to stress that \"futile\" sanctions and pressure will \"never work\" on North Korea, nor will they affect its position as a nuclear weapons state. \"Time proves that the 'sanctions' on the DPRK are doomed to go bankrupt,\" the spokesperson said. DPRK is short for the North's official name, the Democratic People's Republic of Korea. \"(North Korea) vehemently denounces and rejects the U.S. and its vassal forces' ill-intended conspiratorial racket to justify their malicious and depraved hostile policy toward the DPRK under unjust and unreasonable pretexts,\" the spokesperson said. The MSMT was established after a U.N. expert panel, tasked with monitoring sanctions enforcement, was disbanded in April 2024 due to Russia's veto of a resolution to extend its mandate. It consists of 11 countries, including South Korea, the United States, Japan, Australia and Canada",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "kr",
    "eu"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol",
    "ene"
   ],
   "tier": 4,
   "actor": "第三方",
   "alsoUS": false,
