   "title": "N. Korea reports on Swiss FM's visit following opening of diplomatic office",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/foreignaffairs/northkorea/20261031/n-korea-reports-on-swiss-fms-visit-following-opening-of-diplomatic-office",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:42:04 GMT",
   "_dt": 1793414524.0,
   "ageDays": 0.02,
   "summary": "North Korean Foreign Minister Choe Son-hui met one-on-one with her Swiss counterpart visiting Pyongyang earlier this week and discussed promoting dialogue and cooperation, the North's state media reported Saturday. Choe held the talks with Swiss Foreign Minister Ignazio Cassis, who was on a two-day trip since Friday following Switzerland's recent opening of its first diplomatic office in Pyongyang.",
   "summary_zh": "据朝鲜官方媒体报道，朝鲜外务相崔善惠本周早些时候在平壤与到访的瑞士外长一对一会谈，讨论推动对话与合作。崔善惠与瑞士外长伊尼亚齐奥·卡西斯举行会谈。卡西斯自星期五起对朝鲜进行为期两天的访问，此前瑞士刚刚在平壤设立其首个外交办事处。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "North Korean Foreign Minister Choe Son-hui met one-on-one with her Swiss counterpart visiting Pyongyang earlier this week and discussed promoting dialogue and cooperation, the North's state media reported Saturday. Choe held the talks with Swiss Foreign Minister Ignazio Cassis, who was on a two-day trip since Friday following Switzerland's recent opening of its first diplomatic office in Pyongyang. The two sides discussed \"the issue of promoting dialogue and cooperation between the diplomatic fields of the two countries and exchanged the appraisal and views of the international situation of common concern,\" the Korean Central News Agency (KCNA) reported. \"The talks proceeded in a friendly atmosphere,\" the news outlet said, without elaborating. Also attending the talks from the North's side were Jong Tong-hak, the North's vice foreign minister, and Jo Chol-su, North Korea's top envoy to Switzerland, among other officials. In a separate dispatch, the KCNA reported that Cassis paid a courtesy call on Jo Yong-won, secretary of the Central Committee of the Workers' Party of Korea, on the same day. Jo is considered a close aide to North Korean leader Kim Jong-un. Cassis's trip to Pyongyang was followed by his visit to Seoul on Friday. Seoul's foreign ministry said Cassis met with National Security Adviser Wi Sung-lac and separately with Jeong Yeon-doo, vice foreign minister responsible for North Korea affairs, to share details of his discussions in North Korea. Switzerland is a member of the Neutral Nations Supervisory Commission, an independent body established to oversee the enforcement of the Armistice Agreement that ended the 1950-53 Korean War. Switzerland established diplomatic ties with North Korea in 1974, but rather than a formal mission, it operated a humanitarian cooperation office in Pyongyang from 1997 until shutting it down in 2020 amid the COVID-19 pandemic. The opening of the diplomatic office in Pyongyang marks Switzerland's first political and diplomatic presence in North Korea",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "kr",
    "in",
    "eu"
   ],
