   "title": "Facebook Partners Funke Akindele on ‘The Four’",
   "url": "https://www.thisdaylive.com/2026/10/31/facebook-partners-funke-akindele-on-the-four-2/",
   "domain": "thisdaylive.com",
   "source": "ThisDay（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:04:53 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793412293.0,
   "ageDays": 0.05,
   "summary": "is partnering with Nollywood filmmaker and actor Funke Akindele for the London and Lagos premieres of her new film, The Four . “Facebook has always been about connecting people, and our partnership with Funke Akindele brings that to life through film,” Head of Communications, Sub-Saharan Africa, Meta, Oluwasola Obagbemi said.",
   "summary_zh": "正与诺莱坞电影制作人兼演员Funke Akindele合作，为她的新电影《The Four》在伦敦和拉各斯举行首映礼。Meta撒哈拉以南非洲地区传播主管Oluwasola Obagbemi表示：“Facebook一直致力于连接人与人，而我們与Funke Akindele的合作通过电影将这一理念变为现实。”",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "is partnering with Nollywood filmmaker and actor Funke Akindele for the London and Lagos premieres of her new film, The Four . The partnership celebrates Nigerian storytelling and the creators and communities helping it reach audiences around the world. A statement explained that Facebook will support the film’s world premiere in London and its homecoming premiere in Lagos, with experiences that bring creators, celebrities and audiences together. The partnership will show how Facebook helps storytellers connect with fans and build communities around the cultural moments they care about, from film premieres to everyday fandom. “Facebook has always been about connecting people, and our partnership with Funke Akindele brings that to life through film,” Head of Communications, Sub-Saharan Africa, Meta, Oluwasola Obagbemi said. For Akindele, whose career spans acting, producing and directing, the partnership celebrates the audiences who have supported her journey. “African cinema has always had beautiful stories for the world to enjoy, and it’s exciting to have Facebook as a partner in bringing these stories to even more audiences globally,” Akindele said. ’s presence at the Lagos and London premieres will spotlight Nigerian creators at home and in the diaspora, with a creator-hosted space capturing social content on how they use Facebook to connect with younger audiences and share Nigerian stories and culture beyond the country’s borders. “From London to Lagos, the partnership celebrates Nollywood’s global reach and the creators and communities helping Nigerian stories travel,” it added. Founded on January 22, 1995, THISDAY is published by THISDAY NEWSPAPERS LTD., 35 Creek Road Apapa, Lagos, Nigeria with offices in 36 states of Nigeria , the Federal Capital Territory and around the world. It is Nigeria’s most authoritative news media available on all platforms for the political, business, professional and diplomatic elite and broader middle classes while serving as the meeting point of new ideas, culture and technology for the aspirationals and millennials. The newspaper is a public trust dedicated to the pursuit of truth and reason covering a range of issues from breaking news to politics, business, the markets, the arts, sports and community to the crossroads of people and society. You can email us at: hello@thisdaylive.com or visit our contact us page",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "ng"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol"
   ],
   "tier": 4,
   "actor": "第三方",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
   "usHit": false,
