   "published": "Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:56:27 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793411787.0,
   "ageDays": 0.06,
   "summary": "Bandits numbering over 10 have kidnapped four family members at Abangbe Dilu community in Ilorin East Local Government Area of Kwara State. Their abduction has raised serious concerns among their family members, relatives and other residents of the community, who are anxiously hoping for their safe and immediate return. “The people of Abangbe Dilu community remain hopeful that the necessary authorities will respond promptly and that the four abducted family members will return home safely.",
   "summary_zh": "夸拉州伊洛里东地方政府辖区阿邦贝迪卢社区发生绑架事件，超过10名武装分子绑架了4名家庭成员。这次绑架在他们的家人、亲属和社区其他居民中引发严重担忧，大家焦急希望4人平安并立即归来。“阿邦贝迪卢社区居民仍满怀希望，敦促有关当局迅速采取行动，并让4名被绑架的家庭成员平安回家。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Bandits numbering over 10 have kidnapped four family members at Abangbe Dilu community in Ilorin East Local Government Area of Kwara State. The victims, it was learnt, were identified as Hajia Mansurat Musa, her son, Ramadan Musa, Semiu Ahmed, and Sofia Ahmed. Already, the residents of the community have appealed to the federal government to come to the aid of the town in view of the attack. The incident it was gathered happened in the town when the residents of the town were said to be sleeping. Sources close to the town told journalists in Ilorin yesterday that the suspected bandits are yet to contact the families of the victims for the payment of the ransom. Their abduction has raised serious concerns among their family members, relatives and other residents of the community, who are anxiously hoping for their safe and immediate return. A senior police officer with Ilorin East Local Government Divisional Police Headquarters at Oke-Oyi who sought anonymity confirmed the incident to journalists yesterday in Ilorin. “We have been working round the clock to ensure the safe return of the victims,” the source said. The residents of Abangbe Dilu community called on the federal government to come to the aid of the victims. In a statement issued in Ilorin yesterday by the Magaji Abangbe Dilu, Alhaji Jamiu Akanni, appealed to the government and security agencies to intensify efforts to locate the victims and ensure their safe return to their families. They also appealed for improved security measures, effective surveillance and sustained security operations to protect lives and property in the area. “The Kwara State Government is further urged to work closely with relevant federal security agencies, local authorities and community leaders to coordinate efforts towards the safe recovery of the victims.. “The community appeal is for all actions to be guided by the safety and well-being of the abducted persons. “Members of the public are also encouraged to provide credible information to the appropriate security authorities that may assist in the rescue operation. “This is a desperate call for help and urgent intervention. The federal government, Governor AbdulRahman AbdulRazaq and the relevant security agencies are urged to treat the incident with the seriousness it deserves and do everything within their power to ensure that Hajia Mansurat Musa, Ramadan Musa, Semiu Ahmed and Sofia Ahmed are reunited with their loved ones safely and without further delay. “The people of Abangbe Dilu community remain hopeful that the necessary authorities will respond promptly and that the four abducted family members will return home safely. “Our appeal is simple: Please act urgently to bring our people home alive and safe,” he said. Founded on January 22, 1995, THISDAY is published by THISDAY NEWSPAPERS LTD., 35 Creek Road Apapa, Lagos, Nigeria with offices in 36 states of Nigeria , the Federal Capital Territory and around the world. It is Nigeria’s most authoritative news media available on all platforms for the political, business, professional and diplomatic elite and broader middle classes while serving as the meeting point of new ideas, culture and technology for the aspirationals and millennials. The newspaper is a public trust dedicated to the pursuit of truth and reason covering a range of issues from breaking news to politics, business, the markets, the arts, sports and community to the crossroads of people and society. You can email us at: hello@thisdaylive.com or visit our contact us page",
