   "published": "Sat, 31 Oct 2026 07:03:55 +0530",
   "_dt": 1793410435.0,
   "ageDays": 0.07,
   "summary": "Jaishankar strongly disapproved of disruptions in global oil supplies through sanctions and chokepoints, saying deliberate attacks on energy trade and infrastructure were a calculated strategy to hold prices hostage. Mr. Jaishankar’s remarks at the G20 Foreign Ministers’ Meeting in Atlanta on Friday (October 30, 2026) came amid American sanctions on the sale of Iranian oil and disruption to energy supplies from West Asia and the decision to lift sanctions on the sale of Russian diesel.",
   "summary_zh": "贾伊尚卡尔强烈反对通过制裁和封锁点扰乱全球石油供应，称蓄意袭击能源贸易和基础设施是一种calculated策略，意在将价格作为要挟。贾伊尚卡尔先生于2026年10月30日星期五在亚特兰大举行的二十国集团外长会议上发表上述言论。当时，美国正对伊朗石油销售实施制裁，来自西亚的能源供应也受到扰乱，同时俄罗斯柴油销售制裁已被解除。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription External Affairs Minister S. Jaishankar strongly disapproved of disruptions in global oil supplies through sanctions and chokepoints, saying deliberate attacks on energy trade and infrastructure were a calculated strategy to hold prices hostage. Mr. Jaishankar’s remarks at the G20 Foreign Ministers’ Meeting in Atlanta on Friday (October 30, 2026) came amid American sanctions on the sale of Iranian oil and disruption to energy supplies from West Asia and the decision to lift sanctions on the sale of Russian diesel. The Minister said that the world was staring at an energy crisis not of production, but of unpredictability and disruption, unaffordable costs, and challenges of access. Mr. Jaishankar, in a post on X, said he highlighted that deliberate attacks on energy trade and infrastructure were a calculated strategy to hold energy prices hostage. “The G20 must display both understanding and leadership to keep energy markets open and predictable,” he said at the meeting convened by U.S. Secretary of State Marco Rubio. The Minister emphasised that continuous distortions of energy markets through obstacles, sanctions and chokepoints were happening with increasing frequency, greater complexity and wider impact. Mr. Jaishankar said he underscored that there appears to be little regard for the predicament of low-income countries. The Minister said that convenient distinctions are being drawn between oil and gas. “Selective carve-outs speak for themselves,” he said. Mr. Jaishankar said he reiterated that the knock-on effects and mutual dependence in a globalised market should not be underestimated. He reaffirmed that India needs reliable and predictable LPG supplies for its clean cooking needs. Mr. Jaishankar reiterated that India’s National Mission on critical minerals spans exploration to recycling. He also said India has proposed a G20 Critical Minerals Circularity Initiative. The Minister said the G20 must widen access to finance and advance storage, small modular reactors, green hydrogen and biofuels. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
