   "title": "Chinese/Russian deals centered on oil-for-loan financing: China lent tens of billions repaid via discounted crude shipments (often no cash)",
   "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2115337768876253244",
   "snippet": "Chinese/Russian deals centered on oil-for-loan financing: China lent tens of billions repaid via discounted crude shipments (often no cash), with CNPC/Sinopec JVs in underdeveloped fields. Russia used similar loans and Rosneft/Roszarubezhneft stakes for oil prepayments. Goals: secure cheap energy supplies and geopolitical footholds amid sanctions. Venezuela gained credit access but received limited investment, low production gains, and reduced revenue.\n\nThe US deal grants NABEP (US-backed, 35% gov stake) 100-year concessions on 17 fields (~65B barrels, some prior Chinese/Russian ops). Goals: displace rivals, secure crisis reserves/SPR access (20% at cost + first refusal), revive output via up to $100B investment. Venezuela gets royalties/taxes (~$19/bbl, $200B+ projected), jobs, and market-oriented production growth—but faces long-term lock-in and legitimacy questions from opposition.",
   "body": "Chinese/Russian deals centered on oil-for-loan financing: China lent tens of billions repaid via discounted crude shipments (often no cash), with CNPC/Sinopec JVs in underdeveloped fields. Russia used similar loans and Rosneft/Roszarubezhneft stakes for oil prepayments. Goals: secure cheap energy supplies and geopolitical footholds amid sanctions. Venezuela gained credit access but received limited investment, low production gains, and reduced revenue.\n\nThe US deal grants NABEP (US-backed, 35% gov stake) 100-year concessions on 17 fields (~65B barrels, some prior Chinese/Russian ops). Goals: displace rivals, secure crisis reserves/SPR access (20% at cost + first refusal), revive output via up to $100B investment. Venezuela gets royalties/taxes (~$19/bbl, $200B+ projected), jobs, and market-oriented production growth—but faces long-term lock-in and legitimacy questions from opposition.",
